    "4": {
      "note": "The pure model now consumes published explainer categories and grades as inputs. A judgment sort orders each subject's drawn changed blocks by the category's declared scale with the pre-existing Priority order breaking ties, places ungraded blocks last under Ungraded (n), and preserves follower/shared-entry identity. Chips carry explicit presenter-inference hover text with the active category first; carried grades retain all reasons and stale flags. Deterministic sorts remain available, while category sorts are enabled only when their category data exists. The model still authors no judgment: it only renders supplied judgments.\n\nAnchor: `computeLocationJudgment`, `attachJudgmentsAndOrder`, `subjectNode`, `sortOptions`, `changeSetModel`",
      "targets": [
